{
	"$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
	"title": "Image Optimization Patterns",
	"steps": [
		{
			"file": "src/pages/index.astro",
			"description": "Above-fold images are a two-step pattern: import the file from `@assets/images/`, then pass it as a prop (`<Hero image={landingImage} />`). No extra processing needed.",
			"line": 2
		},
		{
			"file": "src/features/demo/Hero.astro",
			"description": "The `image` prop gets passed to Astro's `<Picture>` component. `priority` preloads it (better LCP, less layout shift), and `formats={[\"avif\", \"webp\"]}` generates both — the browser picks whichever it supports.",
			"line": 39
		},
		{
			"file": "src/components/CSPicture/CSPicture.astro",
			"description": "`CSPicture` wraps `<Picture>` for background images — it comes pre-styled with `position: absolute` so it fills its parent container. Use it whenever a CodeStitch component expects a background `<picture>` tag.",
			"line": 13
		},
		{
			"file": "src/features/demo/CTA.astro",
			"description": "The CTA section uses `<CSPicture>` for its background, with `ctaImage` imported from `@assets/images/CTA/`. Storing images under `src/` (not `public/`) is what lets Astro optimize them — `public/` files are served as-is.",
			"line": 8
		},
		{
			"file": "src/features/demo/Hero.astro",
			"description": "## When to use which pattern\n\n| Pattern | Use case |\n|---|---|\n| Import → prop → `<Picture priority>` | Hero/above-fold images that need preloading |\n| `<CSPicture>` | Background images inside stitches that need absolute-positioned wrapper HTML |\n| `<Picture>` directly | Content images needing avif/webp format conversion |\n| `public/assets/` | Logos, SVGs, favicons — files served as-is |",
			"line": 1
		}
	]
}
